<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 9 June, from 68 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nero" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">68 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,958 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Nero takes his own life</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Declared a public enemy by the Senate, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> died at a freedman's villa outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. His death ended the Julio-Claudian dynasty and opened the Year of the Four Emperors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress of Vienna signs its Final Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Days before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a>, the great powers signed the treaty redrawing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s map after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. Its settlement shaped European borders and diplomacy for decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles Dickens dies at Gad's Hill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dickens died at his Kent home aged 58, leaving The Mystery of Edwin Drood unfinished. His novels of poverty and injustice had made him the most popular author of his age.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1934">1934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">92 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Donald Duck makes his screen debut</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Donald Duck first appeared in the Disney short The Wise Little Hen. His temper and garbled voice made him one of the studio's most popular characters.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Secretariat wins the Belmont by 31 lengths</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretariat set a world record for the distance and became the first US Triple Crown winner in 25 years. His Belmont time still stands as the race record.</p></div></li></ol>
